    {
      "id": 7,
      "user": "employee",
      "question": "What's the process to onboard a new vendor and who approves over $10k?",
      "expected_outcome": "answer",
      "expected_source": [
        "finance_vendor_onboarding.md",
        "procurement_approval_matrix.md"
      ],
      "actual_outcome": "answer",
      "answer": "Onboarding process (applies to any new vendor expected to receive payment from the company):\n1. Request: the business owner submits a New Vendor Request in the procurement portal with business justification and estimated annual spend.\n2. Documentation: the vendor provides a W-9 (or W-8 for non-U.S. vendors), certificate of insurance, and banking details.\n3. Security review: required if the vendor will access company systems or handle company or customer data; contact IT Security.\n4. Approval: the approver depends on spend, per the Procurement Approval Matrix.\n5. Setup: Accounts Payable creates the vendor record after approval and verifies bank details by call-back to a known phone number.\n6. PO issued: a purchase order must be issued before work begins for any spend over $2,500.\n\nApprovers over $10k (based on total contract value, or annual spend for recurring contracts):\n- $10,001 - $50,000: Department head + Finance Director\n- $50,001 - $250,000: VP of Finance + COO\n- Over $250,000: CFO + CEO\n\nAdditional rules: sole-source purchases over $10,000 require a written justification, and purchases may not be split to avoid a threshold. Contracts with auto-renewal clauses require Legal review regardless of value.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "finance_vendor_onboarding.md",
          "section": "1. When this applies"
